WEBVTT

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:26.500
Sir Gargantua, can I
hear more of your story?

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:31.100
I can't refuse a request from
such a pretty princess as yourself.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:43.100
My feelings
haven't changed, I swear.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:47.760
I will do anything
you wish, Sir. Gargantua.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:52.030
I accept your sincere words.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:00.300
He's always like that
when he tells this story.

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:03.360
He lives in his memories.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.300
As usual, he never
fails to impress himself.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.160
Sure is.

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:13.730
What?

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:24.300
I want to see you but I can't
see you because it hurts so much.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:28.400
I'm sure I must
be missing something...

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.630
...and that's why my
prayer hasn't been answered.

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:35.730
(Yami, the Hat and the Book traveler)
...and that's why my
prayer hasn't been answered.

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:42.660
I had always believed
that what I saw before me...

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:49.460
...was the only truth there was.

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:57.300
But now I know
there isn't just one world.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:06.830
There are a thousand worlds called
"if" and I don't know which way to turn.

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:12.730
I want to see you but
I can't see you; where are you now?

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:15.860
I'll find you no matter the cost.

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:23.630
I've wandered into the
labyrinth of your eyes.

00:02:23.630 --> 00:02:27.560
Even if the darkness bars my path...

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:33.560
...even if my weak heart
is led astray, I won't give up.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:38.530
I'll keep searching for you.

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:55.200
Leila

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:58.330
I guess when he tells the story that
many times, he gets pretty good at it.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.760
It's become such a
tear-jerker, you know.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:03.500
Do not enter my
castle without permission!

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:04.560
Excuse me?

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:07.160
Who gave you this
castle in the first place?

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:09.830
Go!

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.360
Terrorism is a tyrant's
downfall, Gargantua.

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:21.830
Who cares?

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:24.900
More importantly, when
will you bring me Eve?

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:26.400
Don't scold me.

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:30.100
I'm doing my very best.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:34.530
But I've had no luck yet.

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:35.630
I think it's true.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.630
I'm kinda suspicious.

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:41.060
Shut up!

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:47.600
Before you blame me, think
about what you've done first.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:49.530
What?

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:58.160
You'll never find Eve
with such a clumsy gadget.

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:05.200
What is it with this drawing?

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:08.760
You won't get any clues from this.

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:11.700
My servants did
that on their own.

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:13.160
Master!

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:17.800
I just wanted to
be helpful to you.

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:21.300
Master doesn't like us!

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:28.100
Oh no, you made them cry.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:29.630
You're so terrible.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:34.800
Okay, okay, it's my fault.

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:36.560
Master!

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:38.260
So, you don't hate us?

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:40.200
What about me?

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:44.700
I love you all!

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:48.100
How annoying.

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:52.660
Where are you going?

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:58.060
I was going...
to the ladies room.

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:00.060
That's it, the ladies room!

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:02.400
Don't be fooled by her, master.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:04.700
She tried to escape before.

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:13.760
What is this?

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:17.400
A trap I made just for you.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:21.230
Let me go! I said let me go!

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:23.600
Tell me where Eve is.

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:26.600
I want to know her
whereabouts as well!

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:28.600
Okay, go ahead.

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:41.100
Save me!

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:43.800
I'm so ticklish, I'm gonna die!

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:45.900
Not until you
tell me where Eve is.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:48.100
I told you I don't know!

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:51.700
Why don't we strip her
clothes off and tickle her more?

00:05:53.230 --> 00:05:55.430
That's not a bad idea.

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:57.560
Stop it!

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:17.060
What did you do?

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:19.300
I told you to stop.

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:26.400
It will be 100 million light
years before you catch me!

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:30.960
So, do you really want to die?

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:42.130
Well, I'll forgive you today.

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:46.660
Be careful with this,
if anybody but me or Eve touches it...

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:48.130
See ya!

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:57.800
Wait!

00:06:58.400 --> 00:06:59.700
Master!

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:00.900
Don't go!

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:02.960
Leave me!

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:11.160
I was so close.

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:17.360
Oh, I did it again.

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:20.130
This door is so creaky lately.

00:07:20.930 --> 00:07:24.060
Just pretend you
didn't see anything, okay?

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:25.400
See ya.

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:29.160
Master!

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:38.100
Where are we?

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:42.900
Where are we?

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:49.460
You came here but you
don't know where you are?

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:56.730
Once you enter
the Universal Gardens,...

00:07:56.730 --> 00:07:59.560
...you might be stuck here forever.

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:03.200
What should we do, master!?

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:12.960
Do you want a taste?

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:14.030
Here.

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:25.630
Oh, such a shame, such a shame!

00:08:33.100 --> 00:08:36.960
Sir, a drop of sake is as
precious as a drop of blood.

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:40.900
More importantly, is this
where Lilith disappeared to?

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:44.460
So, you know Lilith?

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:46.400
What's your relationship to her?

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:48.660
I don't have to answer that.

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:52.430
You'll regret that
attitude of yours.

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:55.630
You are trespassers here.

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:02.630
Usually, I would have you
mop the hallway floor for eternity...

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:04.530
...as a penalty but...

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:17.730
What happened?

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:21.760
Now, calm down.

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:35.700
Told you, the doors
are creaky. Be careful.

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:40.630
It hurts!

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:52.860
I told them to be careful...

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:55.560
...real airheads, aren't they?

00:09:57.560 --> 00:09:59.200
What's going on here?

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:03.760
I want to fix it, but I can't
find the right handy man.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:05.630
I'm not asking that.

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:09.830
Why is one space connected
to another by just a door?

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:15.030
Don't bother, just leave it that way.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:22.200
If you're too stiff in your thinking,...

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:26.230
...other parts won't
be stiff when you need them.

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:37.900
Um... they seem to be lost.

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:46.500
Princess Mariel.

00:10:48.430 --> 00:10:52.460
Well, well, by a twist of fate,
it seems Gargantua and Princess Mariel...

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:56.130
...are reunited across
different dimensions.

00:10:56.930 --> 00:10:58.960
How will this end?

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:03.960
With revenge or burning love?

00:11:15.560 --> 00:11:21.660
Pardon me for the sudden interruption
but how about a book world like this?

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:27.300
It is the story that takes
place in the far off, distant future.

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:50.200
Is the basketball regional
elimination game next week?

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:53.530
We play the 16th Block team.

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:55.360
I don't like them.

00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:58.700
We just need to do
our best and beat them.

00:11:58.700 --> 00:11:59.430
That's right!

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:07.600
Leila!

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:11.460
What are you thinking about?

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:13.000
Nothing.

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:15.460
You must be
thinking of Lulan again.

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:17.160
Hey...

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:21.900
...can you imagine what
it's like to drift out in space?

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:29.930
Over 100 years ago, the legendary girl,
Lulan, sacrificed herself...

00:12:30.530 --> 00:12:38.300
...by going outside the spaceship to
repair it. She never made it back.

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:41.560
Did you all get washed?

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:42.630
Yes!

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:44.400
In that case, I'll open the doors now.

00:12:44.900 --> 00:12:47.060
Dry your hair and bodies.

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:57.000
I'm home, mom.

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:58.460
Hi, sweetie.

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:01.300
I scored the highest on
the writing exam today.

00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:04.930
So the teacher gave me an
extra nutritional supplement.

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:06.900
That's very nice.

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:09.130
Good night.

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:12.160
Good night.

00:13:42.430 --> 00:13:43.800
Leila, come here now.

00:13:45.060 --> 00:13:46.100
Emergency call?

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:51.760
Leila?

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:52.960
Lamuro!

00:13:53.360 --> 00:13:54.400
I wonder what this is about?

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:57.660
There's an unidentified
person in the airlock.

00:13:58.030 --> 00:14:00.400
We have to check
it out immediately.

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:11.600
What is this place?

00:14:11.900 --> 00:14:13.300
It's really cramped.

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:16.260
Did you press one of these buttons
here to see if the door might open?

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:22.360
The air is escaping!

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:23.660
Hurry, hit another button!

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:28.300
Oh, you're squishing me!

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:29.860
I can't reach it!

00:14:30.360 --> 00:14:31.830
I am suffering!

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:34.130
It hurts! I'm sensitive to
the change in air pressure!

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:38.060
Keep calm, there's
not a lot of oxygen left.

00:14:42.100 --> 00:14:43.000
I'll open the door.

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:46.630
Hey, can we hold hands?

00:14:47.300 --> 00:14:48.400
Sure but why?

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:49.700
Because.

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:03.700
I thought I was a goner.

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:07.000
Who are you?

00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:09.130
Hi, there.

00:15:16.860 --> 00:15:17.630
Well...

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:20.700
How did you get into this ship?

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:22.430
Ship?

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:25.100
This is the interior
of the space ship.

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:55.930
You could have guessed
because of the air lock system.

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:58.800
I've never seen an
airlock on a spaceship before.

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:02.760
So, you didn't come
from other spaceship?

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:05.130
There is no trace
of any transport.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:06.060
Wow, who's that?

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:07.130
That's Lala.

00:16:07.560 --> 00:16:08.100
Lala?

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:13.330
Never mind this
complicated story for now.

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:15.900
Isn't there some
place to eat here?

00:16:15.900 --> 00:16:16.960
I'm hungry.

00:16:17.430 --> 00:16:19.860
Just ask Lala,
she'll prepare it for you.

00:16:20.430 --> 00:16:21.100
Right?

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:28.330
Guests, please come this way.

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:39.260
It's not bad.

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:41.630
I like this stuff!

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:43.900
It's not real.

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:45.360
It's all synthesized protein.

00:16:45.360 --> 00:16:46.130
I see.

00:16:47.030 --> 00:16:50.430
We've only seen
live animals in videos.

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:53.300
We're hoping to create a
world as soon as we can.

00:16:53.630 --> 00:16:55.100
Create a world?

00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:58.900
Yeah, we were all
born here in this ship.

00:16:58.900 --> 00:17:02.460
When we find the suitable
planet, we'll create our world.

00:17:02.460 --> 00:17:03.860
That's what we were told
by our parents and Lala.

00:17:04.300 --> 00:17:06.100
I see, this is a colony ship?

00:17:06.800 --> 00:17:09.630
Then, we'll be able
to live under the sun.

00:17:12.100 --> 00:17:14.530
By the way Hazuki, don't
you want to eat anything?

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:17.960
I'll get fat by
eating late at night.

00:17:18.360 --> 00:17:22.160
In space, there is no day or
night, you're always stubborn.

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:28.700
Wow, this place
is a mess, isn't it?

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:33.300
There's only one bed, so we
all have to sleep together.

00:17:33.560 --> 00:17:36.230
I'll be wedged in
between your breasts.

00:17:36.230 --> 00:17:37.330
I am worried I might suffocate.

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:42.330
Why, why!?

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:44.830
Why me??

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:51.700
Well, let's share the bed.

00:17:56.530 --> 00:17:58.160
How about a kiss?

00:17:59.060 --> 00:18:00.500
I'll sleep in the hallway.

00:18:04.360 --> 00:18:06.500
Lala is calling both of you.

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:08.500
Something
important to talk about.

00:18:23.130 --> 00:18:23.930
Right this way.

00:18:36.100 --> 00:18:37.760
You two are very mysterious.

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:40.800
In over 200 years,...

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:45.400
...we haven't had other humans
here besides the children born here.

00:18:45.660 --> 00:18:47.260
Oh, I'm flattered.

00:18:47.800 --> 00:18:48.800
What's this about?

00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:51.200
Lately, I've had some concerns.

00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:56.030
9 years ago, all adults
aboard the ship became immobile.

00:18:56.530 --> 00:18:57.860
Immobile?

00:18:58.260 --> 00:18:59.260
Yes.

00:18:59.260 --> 00:19:02.530
The ship's residential
area is divided into 30 blocks...

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:05.360
...and all adults became paralyzed.

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:13.460
Since then, I've taken
care of all the children.

00:19:14.030 --> 00:19:18.960
I taught older children how
to take care of younger ones.

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:21.500
This is block 1.

00:19:21.900 --> 00:19:26.630
There are 15 children per
block with its own school.

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:30.300
I recorded the teachers'
lectures as a holographic video...

00:19:30.300 --> 00:19:33.800
...to educate the
children during this trip.

00:19:34.960 --> 00:19:36.200
That will be all for today.

00:19:36.430 --> 00:19:38.360
Don't forget your homework.

00:19:38.960 --> 00:19:40.030
Yes sir!

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:45.160
She has a crush
on a guy in block 25!

00:19:45.400 --> 00:19:47.730
You said you wouldn't tell!

00:19:47.730 --> 00:19:50.500
Block 25 is the last
one of the spaceship.

00:19:51.300 --> 00:19:53.560
So, it's a long
distance relationship.

00:19:53.560 --> 00:19:54.900
That won't work!

00:19:54.900 --> 00:19:56.700
Yes it will!

00:19:57.160 --> 00:19:59.660
But, it's reaching its limit.

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:04.000
The ship is getting
old and malfunctioning.

00:20:04.960 --> 00:20:06.100
It needs repairs.

00:20:06.360 --> 00:20:11.600
If we can't find a habitable planet
soon, all of our lives will be at risk.

00:20:13.030 --> 00:20:17.800
What do the kids think of
the adults being immobile?

00:20:29.630 --> 00:20:30.260
Here!

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:32.260
Oh, how did you get it?

00:20:32.260 --> 00:20:35.830
Lamuro found it in the
recycle zone at block 6.

00:20:38.830 --> 00:20:41.100
He said that there were
piles of mud in the corner...

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:43.760
...where the flowers bloomed.

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:52.030
Oh, it's beautiful.

00:20:52.260 --> 00:20:53.100
Yes.

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:54.030
I'll go there tomorrow.

00:20:56.700 --> 00:20:59.100
I will bring more for you, okay?

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:00.830
That's something
to look forward to.

00:21:01.830 --> 00:21:02.630
Oh dear?

00:21:05.730 --> 00:21:06.800
Hi there!

00:21:09.400 --> 00:21:11.800
Mother, this is
Lilith and Hazuki.

00:21:14.360 --> 00:21:15.630
This is my mother.

00:21:15.630 --> 00:21:17.130
Nice to meet you.

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:24.660
I have been playing the roles of
their parents for all those years.

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:29.830
I've reproduced their
voices from the records...

00:21:30.030 --> 00:21:33.160
...and make it appear
as if they are speaking.

00:21:46.060 --> 00:21:53.500
I will offer up an eternal prayer.

00:21:53.760 --> 00:21:59.930
I will never give up on what matters.

00:22:02.760 --> 00:22:07.400
I will go there, praying.

00:22:07.960 --> 00:22:14.230
No matter the distance
between us, I will catch you.

00:22:14.500 --> 00:22:22.060
That's a promise between you and I.

00:22:22.260 --> 00:22:29.400
Crying, cradling my memories,...

00:22:29.400 --> 00:22:35.900
...won't help even one
of my feelings to reach you.

00:22:37.500 --> 00:22:44.930
I will offer up an eternal prayer.

00:22:45.130 --> 00:22:51.560
I will never give up on what matters.

00:22:53.530 --> 00:23:00.460
I will find the dawn
between you and I,...

00:23:01.260 --> 00:23:08.900
...and meet the approaching daybreak.

00:23:09.400 --> 00:23:14.130
I will go there, praying.

00:23:15.200 --> 00:23:17.330
Wow, wasn't that scary?

00:23:17.330 --> 00:23:18.200
Wasn't that spooky?

00:23:18.200 --> 00:23:19.060
Wasn't that yucky?

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:22.330
Let's take a look at the next book!

00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:53.930
Next Time: Tamano no Mae
Yami, the Hat and the Book Traveler.

00:23:53.930 --> 00:23:56.960
Enjoy the next story as well.
